Third-party software used by Neura Webdialog
=============================================

This repository does not vendor the packages below. Home Assistant installs
paho-mqtt when the integration is set up. aiohttp is already part of Home
Assistant. The former PHP program and its libraries are not included here.

paho-mqtt
  Project: Eclipse Paho MQTT Python client
  https://github.com/eclipse/paho.mqtt.python
  Authors: Eclipse Foundation and contributors
  License: Eclipse Public License 2.0 OR BSD 3-Clause
  Installed through the integration manifest. Not copied into this repository.

aiohttp
  Project: aiohttp
  https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp
  Authors: aio-libs contributors
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Provided by Home Assistant. Not copied into this repository.

Home Assistant
  https://github.com/home-assistant/core
  Authors: Open Home Foundation and contributors
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Hosts this integration. Not copied into this repository.

Former PHP program
==================

An earlier local PHP script read the same heat-pump page. That script and its
installed libraries are not part of this repository. Their license and author
information is recorded here so the attribution stays with the new integration.

php-mqtt/client 1.8.0
  https://github.com/php-mqtt/client
  Author: Marvin Mall
  License: MIT

phpgt/dom 3.0.3
  https://github.com/PhpGt/Dom
  Authors: Greg Bowler, Alvaro Guimaraes, James Fellows, and contributors
  License: MIT

phpgt/cssxpath 1.1.4
  https://github.com/PhpGt/CssXPath
  Author: Greg Bowler
  License: MIT

phpgt/propfunc 1.0.1
  https://github.com/PhpGt/PropFunc
  Author: Greg Bowler
  License: MIT

guzzlehttp/guzzle 7.5.0
  https://github.com/guzzle/guzzle
  Authors: Michael Dowling, Graham Campbell, Jeremy Lindblom, George Mponos,
  Tobias Nyholm, Márk Sági-Kazár, Tobias Schultze, and contributors
  License: MIT

Transitive dependencies of those PHP libraries (PSR interfaces, Symfony
deprecation contracts, and similar) keep the license and authors published
with each of those projects. They are not shipped in this repository.
